// Starship (full stack) - two-stage methalox super-heavy-lift vehicle.
//
// Simplification: booster and ship are sequential stages; the booster keeps
// the real 3-center / 10-mid-ring / 20-outer-ring Raptor layout at
// representative body-frame stations. Thrust is vacuum-referenced; ambient
// back-pressure is handled by ISP blending in the simulator.
//
// Sources (rough public figures): SpaceX Starship updates - Super Heavy
// ~200 t dry / ~3 400 t propellant, 33 Raptors x ~2 256 kN SL (~7 500 tf
// liftoff); Ship ~110 t dry / ~1 200 t propellant, 3 sea-level + 3 vacuum
// Raptors; Raptor ISP ~327 s (SL) / ~350 s (vac), RVac ~372 s; deep throttle
// to about 40 percent. No payload fairing: payload bay door instead.

